You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "Is the specification document review performed by a single engineer working alone, or does it involve multiple reviewers whose findings must be consolidated before the review is considered complete?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "In what format and location is the specification document stored when it enters the review step — for example, a version-controlled repository, a shared editing platform, or a static file attachment?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "What artifact does the engineer produce to record review findings, and where does that artifact go after the review — for instance, inline annotations, a structured report, or issues logged in a tracking tool?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "What specific criteria or checklist does the engineer use to decide whether a feature is correctly reflected in the document, and what are the possible outcomes of that judgment (e.g., approved, needs minor edits, needs major revision)?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What happens when the engineer discovers a significant gap or blocking issue during the review — for example, is the document sent back to the author, escalated to a lead, or does the review process pause until the issue is resolved?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What triggers a new review instance — for example, a specific event such as a feature branch merge or a release milestone — and roughly how often does this review occur?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Review a specification document for feature coverage, consistency, and editorial errors.",
  "actors": [
    "document reviewer",
    "feature owner",
    "document author",
    "approver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "document repository",
    "change request tracker",
    "review checklist",
    "commenting tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "specification document",
    "feature change list",
    "previous document version",
    "review checklist"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "review comments",
    "change request list",
    "approval decision",
    "updated document"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect document and related change list",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Compare feature changes with document content",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check terminology and formatting consistency",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Record comments and requested revisions",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Revise document based on comments",
      "actor": "document author"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Confirm revisions with feature owner",
      "actor": "feature owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Approve final document",
      "actor": "approver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all feature changes reflected?",
      "branches": [
        "complete",
        "missing changes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are the revisions acceptable?",
      "branches": [
        "approve",
        "request another revision"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing change list",
    "conflicting terminology",
    "unclear feature owner",
    "unresolved comments"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Feature coverage can be checked by comparing change lists and document sections."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Terminology, formatting, and typo checks can be automated."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Review comments can be grouped by section, severity, and owner."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
